   ("The process of photosynthesis", ["Carbon dioxide + water → glucose + oxygen (in the presence of light and chlorophyll).", "Chlorophyll in the chloroplasts traps light energy; the light reaction splits water (photolysis) releasing oxygen; the dark reactions use hydrogen and CO₂ to build glucose.", "The glucose is converted to starch for storage, and used in respiration to release energy.", "Chloroplasts are found mainly in the palisade mesophyll of the leaf; stomata admit CO₂, and the xylem brings water."]),
